--><rss xmlns:sparkle="http://www.andymatuschak.org/xml-namespaces/sparkle" version="2.0"><channel><title>Plato Updates</title><link>https://github.com/fahim-m47/plato-releases</link><description>Plato beta update feed</description><language>en</language><item><title>Plato 0.4.1</title><link>https://github.com/fahim-m47/plato-releases/releases/tag/v0.4.1</link><sparkle:version>0.4.1</sparkle:version><sparkle:shortVersionString>0.4.1</sparkle:shortVersionString><sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion><pubDate>Wed, 05 Aug 2026 21:40:09 -0700</pubDate><description>&lt;h2&gt;Plato 0.4.1&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A small fix so Settings is readable again if your Mac is in Dark Mode.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;Fixed&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;White-on-white controls in Dark Mode.&lt;/b&gt; With macOS set to Dark
  Mode, the Model and Reasoning pickers, the Fast Mode switch, and the
  memory sliders drew white text and knobs on Plato's light paper panel —
  nearly invisible. The panel now always renders its controls in the light
  appearance it was designed for, whatever your system theme.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Permissions, stored keys, and your sign-in all carry over — nothing to
re-grant or re-enter.&lt;/p&gt;</description><enclosure url="https://github.com/fahim-m47/plato-releases/releases/download/v0.4.1/Plato-0.4.1.zip" type="application/octet-stream" length="9055898" sparkle:edSignature="ae9leP9ud6ff47TInTqCdxfEEmVZgWONjLEn6QpIqF59URqXPc+9xJrBygm/WMi1xo5Usv91G3FdQjoQIXj3Cw=="></enclosure></item></channel></rss><!-- sparkle-signatures:
